# .graphifyignore
# Same syntax as .gitignore (including ! negation).
# .gitignore is respected automatically and merged with this file —
# entries here only ever exclude MORE, they never re-include something
# .gitignore already excludes.

# ── graphify's own output — never index its own generated graph ──────────────
graphify-out/

# ── Agent/tool configuration — skill definitions & settings, not book content ─
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.docx-tools/

# ── Standard noise no book project needs in the graph ─────────────────────────
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# ── Secrets — never let these anywhere near the graph ──────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.key
*secret*
*credential*

# Everything else — Chapters Created So Far/, Chats/, Code-bases/, Research/,
# Runs/, and the root .md files (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, Book_Index.md,
# Markdown-Tracking-Guide.md, PROJECT_CONTEXT.md) — is intentionally left
# UNIGNORED. That's the actual source material for the book: raw
# conversations, source code, papers, and dry-run traces are exactly what
# needs to be in the graph for `graphify query`/`path`/`explain` to be useful.
